WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:03.030
Hey guys, it's Jan here.

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:07.770
As always, Game Of Thrones kept up its insane
kill rate in Season 5.

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:10.370
Well, you know "All men must die."

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:14.950
Ok, maybe not all men, but a hell of a lot
of them, and a good deal of women too!

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:19.830
So, in this video I'm going to run through
my five most memorable deaths from this season.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:25.269
But just before I get started, I've got a
great giveaway to celebrate the 10th anniversary

00:00:25.269 --> 00:00:26.750
of our friends at Genki Gear.

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:32.070
To mark the occasion, they've designed 10
cool new T-shirts, including the one I'm wearing,

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:33.490
and you can win one of them!

00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:38.539
All you need to do is be a subscriber and
leave a comment on this video!

00:00:38.539 --> 00:00:44.030
Ok, let's countdown the top five deaths in
Season 5!

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:48.590
The fact he's still alive in the books and
even has a point of view chapter in Winds

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:53.370
of Winter didn't save Ser Barristan Selmy
from getting the chop this season.

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:57.640
Then again showrunners Benioff and Weiss did
send a pretty clear message to A Song Of Ice

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:03.789
And Fire readers in Season 5 when Selyse told
Shireen, 'You have no idea what people will

00:01:03.789 --> 00:01:07.619
do; all your books and you still don't know'.

00:01:07.619 --> 00:01:11.630
Still, we should have known Ser Barristan
was as good as gone when he started reminiscing

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:18.250
about the good old days, waxing lyrical about
the musical exploits of Dany's brother, Rhaegar

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:22.100
Targaryen, and then Dany told him to 'go,
sing a song for me.'

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:27.689
After which the show cut to Hizdahr zo Loraq
saying, 'all men must die, but not all can

00:01:27.689 --> 00:01:28.990
die in glory.'

00:01:28.990 --> 00:01:34.479
At least Ian McElhinney, who plays Ser Barristan,
got his wish for Selmy to go out fighting,

00:01:34.479 --> 00:01:39.509
taking out a slew of Sons of the Harpy before
being fatally wounded.

00:01:39.509 --> 00:01:46.030
Hardhome introduced us to a cool new character,
in the form of female wildling Karsi, before

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:49.710
rudely ripping her away, in typical Game Of
Thrones style!

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:54.930
Yes, after some cracking lines and some kick-ass
action, it was time for Karsi to join the

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:56.420
great ice army.

00:01:56.420 --> 00:02:01.259
Earlier we'd seen her send off her young daughters
on a Night's Watch boat, with the words 'I'm

00:02:01.259 --> 00:02:03.450
right behind you, I promise!'.

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:09.770
So, it was all too horrifyingly fitting that
after she fought off so many eerie attackers,

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:13.020
she was felled by six child wights.

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:18.000
Even though they were basically undead killing
machines, Karsi could NOT bring herself to

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.720
use her weapons against those mini-wights.

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:24.750
But not to worry, thanks to the Night's King,
wildling Karsi's now wight Karsi…

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:30.170
hmmm, why do I get the feeling that this is
all going to end horribly?!

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:35.850
Arya was finally able to cross Kingsguard
Meryn Trant off her hit-list this season,

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:39.960
in a scene that felt like it was straight
out of a horror movie!

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:44.230
Obviously, that's not what Cersei intended
when she sent him off to Braavos with Mace

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.230
Tyrell.

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:50.490
But not only did Trant kill our favourite
sword-master Syrio Forel, he also turned out

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:52.190
to be a child beater and paedophile!

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:57.400
I suppose we could have guessed as he certainly
didn't have any qualms about assaulting Sansa

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:59.100
when Joffrey told him to.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:04.320
Still, that was one hell of a brutal kill
by Arya, stabbing him in the eyes and then

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:09.510
repeatedly in the chest, stomach, and back,
and then finishing him off with a slit to

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:13.590
the throat, which made me think of how her
mother Catelyn killed Walder Frey's wife and

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:16.560
was then killed herself at the Red Wedding.

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:21.100
And I don't think it's any coincidence that
that Season 3 episode and the Season 5 finale

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:24.090
were both directed by David Nutter.

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:29.160
Oh, no, Jon Snow, maybe Ygritte was right
when she said you know nothing!

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:33.310
And obviously he wasn't much of a public speaker
either, otherwise he'd have been able to communicate

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:38.080
just how freakin crucial it was to get the
Wildlings on side in the fight against the

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:39.600
White Walkers!

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:43.200
Actually come to think of it, it's a shame
Jon didn't have a mobile phone and a selfie

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.340
stick during Hardhome.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:48.900
Then he could have snapped a pic or taken
a Vine of himself making a big frowny face

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:53.810
and two thumbs-down, with the Night's King
and the marauding wights in the background.

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:57.730
Maybe that would have convinced the Night's
Watch that Jon was right all along!

00:03:57.730 --> 00:03:59.270
Still, it was not to be.

00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:04.640
Instead, those Stabby McDaggers at the Wall
knifed Jon repeatedly "For The Watch", leaving

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:08.400
our favourite bastard bleeding to death in
the snow.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:11.490
And whose betrayal hurt Jon the most?

00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:14.340
Yes, that potato-boy-turned-Ygritte-killer,
Olly.

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:19.530
Those Men in Black are gonna wish they hadn't
been quite so hasty with their daggers if

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:22.200
the Night's King comes knocking at their gate!

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:25.850
But, hold on, is Jon Snow really dead?!

00:04:25.850 --> 00:04:30.530
If you want to know my theories on that, check
out this video for my Season 6 predictions

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:34.220
for Jon Snow and The Night's Watch!

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:39.720
The award for most heart-breaking death this
season has to go to Shireen Baratheon.

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:44.000
Even though the fact her character was built
up this season meant we knew in our heart

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:49.080
of hearts that something terrible was in store
for her, the whole build-up to her burning

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:51.000
was just shattering...

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:55.870
the touching talk between her and Davos, and
then that conversation with her father in

00:04:55.870 --> 00:04:58.560
which she was SO eager to help him.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:03.670
Add to that the look on Shireen's face when
she saw Melisandre and the pole she was about

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:07.060
to be tied to, and finally realised what was
happening.

00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:10.160
Kerry Ingram gave an incredible performance
as Shireen.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:14.820
Her cries for her father and mother, followed
by her screams were just chilling.

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:21.040
And when her mother, Selyse, who's never been
Team Shireen, tried to stop her daughter's

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:26.460
sacrifice, while Stannis stood by and let
his baby girl burn; that was another very

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:27.610
powerful moment.

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:32.680
As I've said before, what is the world coming
to when Roose Bolton could actually now beat

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:37.070
Stannis Baratheon in a Father Of The Year
contest?!

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:44.830
Ok, just in case Jon Snow somehow isn't dead,
I'm going to include a bonus death!

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:49.330
In the first episode of the season, when the
King-Beyond-The-Wall, Mance Rayder, refused

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:54.430
to kneel to The One True King, Stannis Baratheon,
Melisandre turned the former Night's Watchman

00:05:54.430 --> 00:05:56.380
into a human torch.

00:05:56.380 --> 00:05:58.560
But that was not the end of that.

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:03.740
Wildling lover Jon Snow couldn't bear to watch
Mance go up in flames, so he put him out of

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:05.639
his misery with an arrow to the chest.

00:06:05.639 --> 00:06:10.160
Oh, and there was something in the way the
camera moved during Jon's shooting of Mance

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:13.150
that made me think back to season 4 when Olly
shot Ygritte.

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:18.350
So, what do you think were the most memorable
deaths in season 5?

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:20.520
Let me know in the comments below!

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:26.150
Honourable mentions go to Mossador, the Lord
of Bones, Janos Slynt, the Daznak's Pit fighters

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:31.510
and all those roasted alive and torn apart
by Drogon before he set off on his Never-ending

00:06:31.510 --> 00:06:32.580
Story with Dany.

